							{
								"x" : "-20",
								"y" : "-30",
								"width" : "1200",
								"height" : "460"
							},
							"elements" :
							[
								{
									"item" : "ELEMENT",
									"key" : "flow_text",
									"type" : "flow_text",
									"x" : "0",
									"y" : "0",
									"header_text" : "",
									"text" : "{{P::style_key:page_subheader;&&Navigation}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Moving}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Move the left stick left or right to walk in the desired direction. The further you move the left stick, the faster Kutaro will move.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Crouching}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Hold the left stick down to crouch. Crouching allows Kutaro to avoid some traps and enemy attacks. Remember: sometimes it’s best to keep your head down!}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Jumping}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Press {S} to jump, and continue holding {S} to jump even higher. You can change the direction of Kutaro’s jump by moving the left stick, even while in the air. Kutaro can automatically grab a platform ledge if it’s within his reach after a jump.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Rolling}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Press {W} to roll along the ground. Rolling allows Kutaro to avoid most attacks, even from boss enemies, or escape traps at the last minute. It’s one of Kutaro’s most useful moves for staying alive during his adventure.}}",
									"html" : "",
									"width" : "1150",
									"height" : "240"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"item" : "PAGE",
