							"elements" :
							[
								{
									"item" : "ELEMENT",
									"key" : "flow_text",
									"type" : "flow_text",
									"x" : "0",
									"y" : "0",
									"header_text" : "",
									"text" : "{{P::style_key:page_subheader;&&Investigating}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&<<<ELEMENT::element_key:screenshots/companion;>>>All the world’s a stage in Puppeteer™, and there are many interesting things going on in the background. Kutaro’s magical companions can fly freely around the stage at any time and investigate their surroundings, often yielding additional rewards such as new Heads, Moonsparkles, or other hidden suprises.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&One Player}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Move Kutaro’s companion around the stage with the right stick, and press {R} to investigate or interact with the surrounding area.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Two Players}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&A second player can take control of Kutaro’s companion using a second Wireless Controller, or the PlayStation®Move motion controller, and gain some new abilities over their single-player counterpart.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Use the left stick or point the motion controller to move Kutaro’s companion around the screen, and press {A} or {T} to investigate. The second player can pick up Moonsparkles by touching them, and drop them for Kutaro to pick up by pressing {E} or {G}.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Second player companions can also pick up a loose Head or large Moonsparkle by flying over it and pressing {A} or {T}. Release the item by pressing {A} or {T} again; preferably where Kutaro can easily grab it.}}",
									"html" : "",
									"width" : "1150",
									"height" : "240"
								},
