						{
							"item" : "PAGE",
							"key" : "basic_heads",
							"type" : "free_form",
							"include_in_toc" : "false",
							"is_scrollable" : "true",
							"origin" :
							{
								"x" : "350",
								"y" : "390"
							},
							"mask" :
							{
								"x" : "-20",
								"y" : "-30",
								"width" : "1200",
								"height" : "460"
							},
							"elements" :
							[
								{
									"item" : "ELEMENT",
									"key" : "flow_text",
									"type" : "flow_text",
									"x" : "0",
									"y" : "0",
									"header_text" : "",
									"text" : "{{P::style_key:page_subheader;&&Basic Heads}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Kutaro may have lost his head, but luckily there are plenty of them laying around the world for him to use. Heads are split into two types: basic Heads that can get knocked off of Kutaro’s shoulders when struck by an attack, and Hero Heads that bestow Kutaro with special abilities and stick with him forever.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Basic Heads can be found all over the place, and each has its own unique ability. Kutaro may hold on to three basic Heads at once and switch between them freely by pressing directional button {◀} or {▶}. Acquiring a fourth head will replace Kutaro’s current head with the new one.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Kutaro’s current Head is knocked off of his body when struck by an enemy attack. Make contact with the Head quickly to get it back, otherwise it disappears after a short amount of time and Kutaro equips one of his remaining Heads. Kutaro loses a life when he loses his final Head.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Head Actions}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&<<<ELEMENT::element_key:screenshots/heads;>>>Each basic Head has a unique Head Action, activated by pressing directional button {▼}. Head Actions can be used to unlock hidden paths, Bonus Stages, or uncover hidden items. Look for symbols in the environment that match the Head icons displayed in the upper-left corner of the screen and, if you have the matching Head, activate your Head Action to uncover its secrets.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Note that the Head you need to access a hidden area might not be available in the current stage. Kutaro keeps his collection of Heads between levels, so try replaying the stage later with the correct Head to see what you missed.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Powers}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&There are many legends in the Moon Kingdom that speak of mighty warriors who nobly defended against the Moon Bear King’s uprising. Kutaro can make their powers his own along his adventure.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Guard}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&<<<ELEMENT::element_key:screenshots/guard;>>>Kutaro can defend against enemy attacks and deflect enemy projectiles after acquiring the Knight’s powers. Hold {Q} to create a magical shield around Kutaro and move the left stick to change the direction of reflected projectiles.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Kutaro’s shield can withstand three hits before requiring time to recharge. The shield changes color from blue to yellow to red with each hit. His shield recharges automatically when not in use.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Ninja Bomb}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&<<<ELEMENT::element_key:screenshots/ninjabomb;>>>Kutaro can summon bombs at will once he has claimed the Ninja’s powers. Press {A} to throw a bomb, or hold the left stick down and press {A} to drop a bomb at his feet.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&Keep an eye out for bomb icons drawn on the environment. These icons indicate areas that can be blown up for extra rewards and surprises.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Hook Claw}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&<<<ELEMENT::element_key:screenshots/hookclaw;>>>The Hook Claw ability, acquired by the getting the Pirate’s powers, allows Kutaro to attach himself to hooks and other objects in the environment. Hold the left stick in the direction of your target and press {D} to fire the Hook Claw.}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_bold;&&Body Slam Attack}}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&& }}{{P::style_key:page_normal;&&<<<ELEMENT::element_key:screenshots/bodyslam;>>>The Wrestler’s powers give Kutaro the ability to perform a powerful Body Slam Attack on the ground below his feet by pressing {E}. Like with the Ninja Bomb, look for bull icons in the environment to find hidden areas or items that can be accessed with the Body Slam Attack.}}",
									"html" : "",
									"width" : "1150",
									"height" : "240"
								},
								{
									"item" : "ELEMENT",
									"key" : "screenshots/heads",
									"type" : "image",
									"x" : "0",
									"y" : "0",
									"header_text" : "",
									"text" : "",
